WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.712
Before calculating with an array, inspect its structure.

00:00:03.712 --> 00:00:06.977
Four properties are especially useful.

00:00:06.977 --> 00:00:11.102
Data type tells us what kind of values are stored.

00:00:11.102 --> 00:00:14.762
Shape tells us the size of each dimension.

00:00:14.762 --> 00:00:21.562
Number of dimensions tells us whether the array is one dimensional, two dimensional, or higher.

00:00:21.562 --> 00:00:25.072
Size tells us the total number of values.

00:00:25.551 --> 00:00:32.572
For example, an array with three rows and four columns has a shape of three by four, two dimensions,

00:00:32.572 --> 00:00:39.162
and twelve total elements. These properties are simple, but they are extremely important.

00:00:39.162 --> 00:00:46.820
If a calculation produces an unexpected result, checking the shape and data type is often the first debugging step.
